# counter harness. One call is one full-dataset loss and gradient.
# An L-BFGS-B line-search request and an LM error retry each count.
# A repeated weight vector is cached and is not counted again.
# Success requires every parameter-tensor gradient L2 at or below the stop, with the call count under the cap.
# pyamff 8037eb98 stopped on the max absolute entry of each tensor. This row uses the L2 test.
# There is no weight-space Hessian, so wrong_stationary is unused.
# mean_epoch is the half-even mean of the successful call counts.
# RMSE means are arithmetic means of the successes. force_rmse is -1 when the force coefficient is 0.
# Behler-Parrinello squared-error loss on the problem trajectory. Fingerprints come from the archived fpParas.dat. The network has hidden layers 10 and 7, tanh, and a linear output, with NoScaler. Each start is uniform[-1, 1) from PCG64(20261015 + index). One harness call is one full-dataset loss and gradient. The stop is the L2 norm of each parameter-tensor gradient. pyamff 8037eb98 used the max absolute entry. The extended Kalman filter uses lambda 0.999, lambda0 0.97, state 10, pnoise 0, and wgroup 100. The covariance starts at 0.1 on the diagonal and 0 off the diagonal. One call walks every structure, and every force residual when the force coefficient is positive. The force coefficient is 0, so force RMSE is -1. The stop is 0.02 and the cap is 10000.
problem mlopt/C2H4
mean_force_rmse -1.0
median_force_rmse -1.0
nfailed 32
